abstract: |
  MIS v2.1 introduces revolutionary token-based security orchestration for autonomous 
  AI agents with three key innovations: (1) cryptographic capability tokens validated 
  in eBPF kernel space achieving sub-100 nanosecond latency—200x faster than traditional 
  access control mechanisms; (2) intent-driven execution contracts that automatically 
  resolve high-level goals (e.g., "RESEARCH", "DEPLOY") into fine-grained permissions; 
  (3) distributed session orchestration supporting live migration and zero-downtime 
  updates. Performance benchmarks demonstrate 42x improvement over v2.0, supporting 
  2000+ concurrent agent sessions per node with <0.5% CPU overhead. Released under 
  MIT license as a reference architecture enabling both academic research and commercial 
  production systems. This work addresses critical challenges in AI safety, autonomous 
  agent security, and embodied learning systems.

